Upstream ggml-org/llama.cpp 7f24aacde (#29810, "cpu: accumulate flash attention V in F32"), MIT.
The CPU flash attention kernel that runs below the 64-query tile (and in the split-KV decode path) kept the running
V sum of an F16 V cache in F16 and normalized it only at the end. With enough keys the unnormalized sum passes 65504
and the output is inf / NaN although every V value and the true output are small; below that it still rounds every
partial sum to F16. Every V type now accumulates in F32 like the tiled kernel; F16 rows are widened in-register by
ggml_vec_mad_f16_f32 (AVX512, AVX + F16C, NEON, RVV, scalar). The tiled kernel (64+ queries, the diffusion DiT and
VAE attention) is unchanged. Adds test-fa-f16-v-accum (the CPU kernel vs a double-precision reference; test-backend-ops
uses the CPU backend as its reference and cannot see this).

